    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d58">

                <pb facs="0200" n="166" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v09/pg166"/>

                <head>58. Memorandum From the President’s Special Assistant (Rostow) to President
                        Johnson<anchor n="1" xml:id="d58-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1966-11-16">November 16, 1966</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I recommend your approval of this determination permitting the internal transfer
                    of AID funds in support of expanded administrative expenses in AID’s Vietnam
                        program.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d58-f2"/>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0201" n="167" xml:id="pg167"/>
                <p>The amount involved is $5 million. Congress authorized AID to transfer up to that
                    amount from its Supporting Assistance account to its Administrative Expenses
                    account in FY 1966; in compliance with the Foreign Assistance Act you approved a
                    determination in June, 1966 that the transfer was necessary for the purposes of
                    the act.</p>
                <p>Congress authorized the same procedure for FY 1967, subject again to your
                    determination that it is necessary.</p>
                <p> BOB has verified AID’s continuing need for this internal transfer.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d58-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Walt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d58-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d58-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Johnson Library, National Security File, Subject File, Presidential
                    Determinations, Vol. IV [2 of 2], Box 40. No classification marking.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d58-f2" n="2" xml:id="d58-f2-content">
                <p>The determination attached to the source text has not been found.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d58-f3" n="3" xml:id="d58-f3-content">
                <p>A November 14 memorandum from Schultze to President Johnson reads in part: “Our
                    review indicates that AID will need the authorized $5,000,000 for administrative
                    expenses to carry out expanded programs in Vietnam.” He recommended that the
                    President sign the determination. (Ibid.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
